  <data name="OnboardingShareTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Back up and share</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnboardingShareBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In Settings, the Import / Export screen saves your campaigns and sounds to a .dmpack file: to back them up, find them on another device, or share them with other GMs.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourCampaignIntroTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your campaigns</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourCampaignIntroBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This screen organizes your games. A campaign is split into chapters, and each chapter into scenes. A scene gathers the tracks that play together: launch it from here to open it in the mixer.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourChevronTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Expand or collapse</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourChevronBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The chevron expands or collapses the campaign. Tapping the rest of the row only expands it, never collapses it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourCampaignHandleTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Reorder</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourCampaignHandleBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Drag the handle to reorder your campaigns. Chapters and scenes have the same handle.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSessionTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A chapter</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSessionBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A chapter groups scenes, for example those of one game session. Tap it to show its scenes.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSceneTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A scene</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSceneBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A scene is a soundscape ready to play: its tracks, their volumes, and their settings. Tap it to select it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourCreateTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourCreateBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Add a campaign, chapter, or scene. The type and location are prefilled from the selected row, and you can change them.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourEditTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Edit</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourEditBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Rename the selected row. A chapter or scene can also be moved to another campaign or chapter.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourDeleteTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Delete</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourDeleteBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Deletes the selected row after confirmation. Deleting a campaign or chapter also deletes everything in it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourLibraryIntroTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Library</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourLibraryIntroBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>All your sounds live here: music, ambiences, and sound effects, sorted by category. These are the tracks you then put in your scenes' channels.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourMixerIntroTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The mixer</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourMixerIntroBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This is where you play a scene. Each channel runs one track at its own volume: layer them to build the soundscape, and switch scenes during the game.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourMixerChannelBackgroundTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The strip background</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourMixerChannelBackgroundBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>It lights up during playback and follows the actual volume: it rises during a fade-in and drops during a fade-out. The bands at the top and bottom show that a fade-out or fade-in is set.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSettingsIntroTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Channel settings</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSettingsIntroBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>These settings apply to this channel in this scene. “Save” keeps them, “Cancel” leaves everything as it was.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSettingsVolumeTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Volume</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSettingsVolumeBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This channel's volume in the scene, the same as on the strip.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSettingsLoopTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Loop</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSettingsLoopBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The track starts over when it ends, for a never-ending soundscape.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSettingsFadeInTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Fade in</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSettingsFadeInBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When it starts, the volume rises gradually instead of starting all at once.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSettingsFadeOutTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Fade out</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSettingsFadeOutBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When it stops or the scene changes, the volume lowers gradually before cutting off.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSettingsAutoPlayTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Autoplay</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourSettingsAutoPlayBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The track starts on its own when the scene is launched.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourImportExportIntroTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Import / Export</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourImportExportIntroBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This screen backs up and shares your work through .dmpack files. The summary at the top of the screen sums it up at any time; here are its two blocks.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourExportLevelTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>What to export</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourExportLevelBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Structure only: the campaign, its chapters, and its scenes, without sound. Structure + channels: the same with each scene's channels and the audio they use. Audio library only: all your tracks, without campaigns. Full backup: everything.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourExportCampaignTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Which campaign</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourExportCampaignBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>For “Structure only” and “Structure + channels”, pick the campaign to export. The other two levels cover the whole app, so this row disappears.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TourExportTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Export</value>
  </data>
